1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,140
 Why is AI so bad at writing content, despite all of the YouTube videos and viral hooks that you've fed?

2
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:08,540
 Well, it's because all Claude actually takes from those videos is the steps.

3
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:09,900
 Step one, make a bold claim.

4
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:11,280
 Step two, numbered list.

5
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:12,360
 Step three, CTA.

6
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:15,720
 It just blindly copies the steps, but completely misses the thinking behind it.

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:21,160
 The fix I found that works pretty well is to stop giving Claude steps altogether and instead teach it how to think.

8
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:25,660
 Welcome to Skill of the Week, ladies and gentlemen, where every week I share with you one useful agent skill.

9
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:29,760
 This week's skill is called Content Principles, and it is made by yours truly.

10
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:35,220
 I've spent over 500 hours studying the grades of short-form content and distilled everything that I've learned into one skill.

11
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:39,200
 Opening curiosity loops, using specificity, line one has to sell line two, and so on.

12
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:41,060
 Simply use this skill while making any content.

13
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:44,640
 I like it for scripting videos, or you can ask Claude to use that skill to audit your existing work.

14
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:47,560
 I now use this skill for every single piece of content that I produce.

15
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:54,220
 In just the last 30 days, when I've really dialed in the skill, I've doubled my views to 1.8 million and gained an additional 12,000 followers.

16
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:56,440
 And more importantly, my videos don't feel like AI slots.

17
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:00,040
 I shouldn't even be doing this, but if you want access, comment the word skill down below

18
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:00,920
 and I'll send it over to you.

